WEBVTT

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.880
<i>That day, that time...</i>

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.260
<i>We were thrown into the future,
into the year 2388.</i>

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.430
<i>Waiting for us in the future
was the organization called Revisions.</i>

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.140
<i>The AHRV fights against the Revisions.</i>

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.640
<i>They gave us weapons
called String Puppets.</i>

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.150
<i>We devoted ourselves
to protecting everyone using it.</i>

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.150
<i>But to save the people
who had been abducted,</i>

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.070
<i>we ended up attacking the Revisions' base.</i>

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.870
I see. Milo was able to join you.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.290
<i>Officer Izumi.</i>

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.200
Yes, sir?

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.790
<i>Sorry, I know this will be difficult.</i>

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.250
<i>I want everyone
to come back alive and safe!</i>

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:47.750
Yes, sir.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.170
I promise to make this
Operation Nephilim succeed.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.650
All we adults can do is sit here and wait

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.940
while we entrust everything
to the children.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.200
I can't get over this feeling.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.660
Same here.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:44.620
It's hard to for me to grasp the balance

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.290
between my title as Chief
and what I can actually do.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.630
So, even the tough-looking Chief Kuroiwa
can be helpless.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.590
This is no time for kidding.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:54.840
Chief Kuroiwa,

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.170
will you allow me to examine

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.260
the enemies' corpses
and assemble a research team?

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.300
I want to do whatever I can

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.560
while we're here,
so when we return to our time,

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.850
we can respond in some way
to the impending epidemic.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.350
I would appreciate that, Dr. Dojima.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.440
I need your help.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.900
<i>Practical research may have to wait</i>

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.110
<i>until we return to our time.</i>

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.910
<i>For now, let's just trust that Daisuke and
the others will succeed on their mission.</i>

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.410
That might even be taller
than Tokyo Skytree.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.500
So, that's the enemy's base.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.590
Milo, do we have a concrete plan?

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.300
We in AHRV had a general idea
of its whereabouts,

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:43.300
but we never came this close,
let alone infiltrated it.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.060
That's because we never had anything
that had a chance of defeating them.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.350
So, Mom is in there.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.020
You mean we don't have a plan?

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.020
That's right.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:55.610
Lu,

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.940
the Revisions aren't expecting us
to attack them.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.400
That's why,

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.240
we'll win by surprise attack!

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.410
There you go again, getting carried away.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:05.780
Get serious, will you?

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.200
-Doesn't that sound brave?
-What?

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.330
Daisuke is going to protect
all of us, right?

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.250
What? Oh, yes! Leave it to me!

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.080
Milo, what do you think?

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:14.830
It's as Daisuke says.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.880
Right now,

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.880
we have the String Puppets
and you, the String Masters.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.840
Did you hear that, Gai?

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:22.800
However,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.220
this operation
is not part of AHRV's plans,

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.470
and our lives will be in danger.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.100
But besides their disease,

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.730
the Revisions have
no other natural enemies.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.690
The AHRV doesn't even have a base.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.560
It appears their security is light.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.480
So, how will we infiltrate?

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.940
Why don't we go
right through the front door?

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:45.240
Are you nuts?
This is the enemy's base, you know!

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.820
No, he's right.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:50.120
Mikio Dojima escaped, so if we follow
the route he told us about,

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.330
we should be able to reach
the other abductees.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.660
That will work!

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.540
But then there's also the artificial
quantum brain Milo mentioned.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.960
To be honest,
we'll just have to search for that.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:05.630
But since I have the same kind of brain,
I can sense it.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:08.680
If you find it, Milo, and we destroy it,

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.810
then we can return to our time, right?

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:11.720
Yes.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:15.310
But if you're not in Shibuya
when it's destroyed,

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.650
you'll be left behind in this time.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.940
So, even if we save
everyone else, we will...

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.480
Is there no other way?

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:23.440
There is.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.120
When we find where the artificial
quantum brain is, we'll plant it there.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.120
A bomb?

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:34.200
Then, if you detonate it
after you've returned to Shibuya...

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.620
We can also...

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:36.870
Return.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.790
Okay. We'll split into two teams.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.670
Daisuke, Keisuke, Izumi, Marimari.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:44.920
Yes?

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:49.890
Your team's goal is
to retrace the route Mikio Dojima told us

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:51.970
and rescue the hostages.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:53.140
Sure.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.770
After rescuing the hostages,
lead them out and return to Shibuya.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.060
Then, Gai and Lu,

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:05.610
the three of us will search
for the artificial quantum brain.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.360
When we find it, we'll plant the bomb,

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:10.820
then immediately escape
and return to Shibuya.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.990
As soon as we confirm
that everyone is safe, we'll detonate it.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:15.580
That's the plan.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:16.750
-Roger.
-Got it.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:19.870
Wait a minute, guys.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.630
What is it?

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.510
This kind of thing makes me
somewhat thrilled.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.970
Come on, say something, Daisuke.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.930
Well...

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.560
There's a lot of things
I want to tell you guys, but...

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.730
Anyway,

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.020
thank you for giving me this chance.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.190
What's with you? I wasn't expecting that.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.440
I kept screwing up lately.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.160
But I believe in my destiny.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:52.370
So, I want you to believe too.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.370
Believe in you?

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:56.160
No, I mean, in my destiny.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.620
Looks like all that stupid stuff
Daisuke has said since way back then

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:00.960
all came true.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:05.000
Well, without that, there would be nothing
to remember Daisuke for.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.050
You can be cruel sometimes.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:12.680
Normally, I'm unlucky,
but I feel pretty good today.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:15.510
I mean, I think I can do what I need to.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.930
Not just rescuing my mom,

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.810
but also bringing back everyone else
that was abducted.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.520
Luck will follow if I do what I need to.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.320
I love all of you.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.610
So, I believe that

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.530
whatever happens today
will be a good memory.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:35.240
Thank you for believing in me
at the police station, Marimari.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:37.080
What? Sure.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.160
Thank you for doing your best
all this time.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.790
I'll do my best today too.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.710
You're always doing your best, Ms. Izumi.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:45.840
That's right.

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:50.260
Actually, I have a dream I want to pursue.

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:54.390
There are a lot of things I want to do
when I return to our time.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.010
So I'll do my best today.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:58.930
You too, Gai.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.230
What? Well...

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:04.270
When I think about how the future
of everyone in Shibuya depends on us...

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.190
Don't worry.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:08.440
Your sister knows
just how much you can do, Gai.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:09.940
We're counting on you.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.280
Then, I have one thing to say.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.950
I'm not going to depend on
what Daisuke calls "destiny."

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.910
I trust in our strength
to get us through this,

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.960
so we can all return alive.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:23.870
Do you understand, Daisuke?

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:24.790
You bet.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:26.840
You say something too, Milo.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.170
We've come this far, so we'll make
this operation succeed somehow.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:34.220
That's why I'm here.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:35.390
That's right.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.390
I swear we'll succeed.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.100
Then, just like Marimari said,
this will make a good memory.

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:42.600
All right!

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.560
For the success of Operation Nephilim!

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.110
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:56.910
Milo.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.080
Just you watch.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.830
All right. I'm counting on you.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.790
Let's do this!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.260
What do you mean all the String Puppets
have been dispatched?

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:13.880
I take full responsibility!

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.630
That's not the problem!

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.390
Isn't it the police's duty
to guarantee the safety

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:20.060
of the citizens in the disaster area?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.730
Do you think if we just wait here,
we'll all survive?

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:27.690
We have hardly
any food or electricity left.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.860
We can't rely only on those kids.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.400
We have to do whatever we can too!

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:42.700
I find it hard to believe
that AHRV is planning to attack us.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:46.580
They must have gotten cocky
after making those weapons.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:47.870
It ticks me off.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.210
We should be careful though.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.090
This is no time for that.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.840
That's right. Why can't we just ignore it?

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.350
You're too much of a coward,
you fake doggy.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:02.930
I'm not a fake doggy.

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:05.180
-My last name is Nico, member of Laos.
-Right. Shut up.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:08.480
-People call me--
-You need to learn your place.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.730
That's right.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.110
As the saviors of the Revisions,

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.650
the time is over
when you can speak to us as equals.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.900
Oh, where are you going, king doggy?

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:21.030
I'm just going to mess with
my favorite boy.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.790
-We're acquaintances, after all.
-Why, you!

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:26.290
What's with that damn mutt?

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:28.080
Let him do as he pleases.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.380
<i>His real body is protecting us.</i>

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.500
<i>He may be of low status,
but he has great combat skills.</i>

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:37.630
Besides, we can't be
involved in trivial things.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:38.760
That's for sure.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.550
Your new body
is complete as well, Chiharu.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:44.640
It won't be long now.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.310
We sisters

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:49.440
will become the light
for our comrades whose destiny

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.150
is to be trapped
in the darkness and perish!

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:01.820
There aren't any enemies at all.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.450
Yes. It's kind of a letdown.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:05.540
<i>You two!</i>

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.580
Don't let your guard down!

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:11.080
Ms. Izumi,
according to what Daisuke's uncle told us,

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:14.420
the abductees are imprisoned
up ahead on the left.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:17.550
Okay! Let's rush in
before we run into the enemies.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.800
<i>Daisuke! The left! Watch the left side!</i>

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.600
I can hear you, Ms. Izumi. Settle down.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:30.180
How is it going, Milo?
Do you sense anything?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.400
No, not yet.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.650
To be honest, I'm only taking a chance

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.230
that my brain will detect
their artificial quantum brain.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.240
You sounded confident earlier.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.280
Was I supposed to make everyone
feel uneasy at a time like that?

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:44.700
There you go again!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.950
That's what ticks everyone off about you.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.290
Why don't you just say, "I don't know,"
when you don't know?

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:51.750
Sorry.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.830
I've never been in contact with people
except during missions.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:57.420
I'm sorry if I've hurt your feelings.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.300
Forget it.

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:00.880
I also went too far.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.970
<i>Four enemy heat signatures detected ahead.</i>

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:07.760
So, the enemy team has arrived!

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:14.100
According to
Mr. Dojima's information, it's here.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.810
I don't see anyone around.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.020
Let's split up.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:26.990
There are people here!

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.410
They're alive!

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:29.700
All right!

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.330
Step back, everyone!

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.290
-What?
-What's that?

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.930
Everyone, this is the police.
We've come to rescue you.

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:45.930
It's the police!

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:47.390
You'll get us out of here?

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:49.850
Mom? Where's my mom?

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.690
Thank goodness! We've been saved.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:59.610
Hurry up, and get us out of here!

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:01.400
We can return to Shibuya!

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.780
That should be all of them.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.110
Mom! Answer me!

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.620
-Mom!
-Keisaku.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.990
Did you find her?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.080
They say that there's a chance
this is not everyone who was captured.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.290
Oh, that's right.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:22.760
Right. There's no way of confirming
if this is everyone or not.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:26.550
It seems that Keisaku's mother
is not here.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:27.970
<i>Roger that.</i>

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.470
<i>At any rate, start the evacuation. Got it?</i>

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:34.230
Ms. Izumi!

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.230
I'll search a little farther ahead.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:40.190
Okay.

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:43.690
We'll start leading everyone out,
so we can get the evacuation going.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:45.400
Don't do anything reckless.

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:46.650
I won't.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:49.450
Keisaku.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:51.950
I'm sure we'll find your mother.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.450
Yes. Thank you, Marimari.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:06.170
<i>There weren't that many of them.</i>

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:08.970
Right. That didn't seem
their interception force.

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:12.760
We just happened to run into
these Civilians on regular patrol.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:13.930
That's what it seems like.

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:16.890
<i>Cut it out with the killing spree, AHRV.</i>

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:20.020
<i>You're murdering our innocent comrades.</i>

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:22.690
<i>You're nothing more than evil beasts.</i>

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:23.860
I know that voice.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:28.740
<i>It won't be long before our plan succeeds.</i>

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:32.700
<i>This is such a great opportunity,
I think I'll invite you to watch.</i>

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:36.330
We're not going, right?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.040
No, this is our chance.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:41.040
Yes. We'll have a better chance
of detecting the artificial quantum brain.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.000
Darn! You sure like a challenge.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:47.510
<i>Yes. Come up to us.</i>

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.140
What is this place?

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:58.140
Have you been lonesome, lonely boy?

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:00.400
You're back again, you jerk?

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:04.270
Hey! Where's my mom?
Give her back right now!

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:09.320
The youngsters of 2017
are a bunch of rude kids!

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.160
No, not only you are rude,

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:12.820
you even let the captives go earlier,

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:15.740
<i>the people you think are our ancestors.</i>

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:16.990
<i>"Earlier"?</i>

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.870
<i>You mean the people we released?</i>

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.840
Everyone besides them
are important materials.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:28.210
But we're counting down
to a big event right now.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:31.510
You lonely boy, and you too, lonely boy,

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.640
behave yourselves.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.470
Mom!

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.720
Farewell!

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:40.180
You jerk!

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:44.690
You really are a hopeless one.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:47.230
But you know, I don't mind

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:48.940
this kind of play.

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:53.610
So, for you, lonely boys,

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:59.540
I'll show you something interesting
to celebrate this occasion.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.710
Are you Nicholas?

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:15.470
Mom!

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.350
<i>Emergency!
Gravitational irregularity detected.</i>

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:21.430
-Keisaku...
<i>-It's recommended to leave immediately.</i>

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:25.810
<i>It's recommended to leave immediately.</i>

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:34.450
Mom!

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:38.330
It's hopeless, Keisaku! We'll die!

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.120
Who cares?

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:43.000
Mom!

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.500
Mom!

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.090
No...

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:53.300
No!

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:58.970
These materials are the sustenance
that provides us with life.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:01.850
Thank you.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.640
I bid you farewell. Ta-ta.

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:27.040
Keisaku.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:30.000
Let me do it! I'll kill him!

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:32.000
Stop!

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:33.460
Keisaku!

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:35.220
Keisaku!

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:39.800
This is the first time anyone
from AHRV has ever been here.

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:41.560
You should feel honored.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:42.850
Amazing, isn't it?

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:46.850
It was built from the brains
of your AHRV comrades.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:48.520
Who knew it was so huge?

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:50.520
-Milo?
-I'm all right.

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:52.280
My quantum brain

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:55.070
and that artificial quantum brain
are resonating with each other.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:57.530
Gai.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:00.240
Separate the enemy as much as possible
and confuse them.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.830
<i>I'll plant the bomb
while they're distracted.</i>

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:03.950
Roger.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:06.830
Lu, the one who we think is
controlling the quantum brain,

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.120
go after that Revision.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:10.670
What are you whispering about?

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:12.420
It's useless, you know.

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:15.800
<i>Emergency!
Gravitational irregularity detected.</i>

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:19.720
-You won't be fighting here today, boy.
<i>-It's recommended to leave</i>

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.260
<i>-immediately.</i>
-Gai!

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:25.890
It won't be long now.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:27.850
Watch closely.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:30.810
Your friends were used as the materials

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:33.770
that will give birth
to Chiharu's new body.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:55.050
Do you see now?
The power of this artificial quantum brain

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:59.260
and the quantum brain
in the reborn Chiharu

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:04.560
will hold the 2017 Shibuya right here.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:07.480
This will save humanity!

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:10.390
What a joy! Congratulations, humanity!

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.190
Now, the only advantage AHRV is...

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:20.240
I'm surprised you caught up.
Now take this.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.580
Chiharu!

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:27.540
Keisaku.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.920
What the hell is this?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:40.880
You bitch!

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:44.760
You're the asshole
who kidnapped my mother!

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:49.060
You must be kidding me!
How can this be happening?

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:50.980
I...

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:55.440
I am supposed to leap to the past
and become the light to my comrades!

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.780
Don't!

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:17.090
-What?
-No!

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:18.920
Retreat!

00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:03.320
<i>Yes. We'll be arriving in Shibuya shortly.</i>

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:05.110
<i>We have about 60 people.</i>

00:22:05.990 --> 00:22:09.280
<i>Yes. We failed to demolish
the artificial quantum brain.</i>

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:14.830
<i>According to Milo,
when Keisaku defeated their secret weapon,</i>

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:18.290
<i>he prevented the Shibuya of 2017 and 2388</i>

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>from permanently switching places.</i>

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:24.460
<i>But Keisaku is...</i>

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:38.440
<i>In the end, I couldn't even fulfill
the destiny I've always believed in.</i>

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:41.060
<i>I'm the worst loser on earth.</i>

00:22:41.980 --> 00:22:44.440
<i>My destiny to protect everyone</i>

00:22:45.150 --> 00:22:47.400
<i>came to an end today.</i>

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:51.990
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
